 "grammar": {
  "title": {
   "ko": "식당 표현: I'll have... / Could I have...? / I'd like...",
   "en": "ordering food: I'll have, Could I have and I'd like"
  },
  "explain": {
   "ko": "식당에서 주문할 때는 I'll have + 음식 또는 I'd like + 음식을 씁니다. 부탁할 때는 Could I have ..., please?, 계산은 Could we have the bill, please?라고 합니다. 직원은 Are you ready to order? / What would you like?라고 묻습니다.",
   "en": "To order use I'll have + food or I'd like + food. To ask for something say Could I have ..., please? To pay say Could we have the bill, please? The waiter asks Are you ready to order? / What would you like?"
  },
  "table": {
   "head": [
    "표현 / Pattern",
    "예 / Example"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "주문 / ordering",
     "I'll have the fish. I'd like soup."
    ],
    [
     "부탁 / asking",
     "Could I have water, please?"
    ],
    [
     "계산 / paying",
     "Could we have the bill, please?"
    ],
    [
     "질문 / questions",
     "Are you ready to order? What would you like?"
    ]
   ]
  },
  "notes": [
   {
    "ko": "주문은 I'll have ... 또는 I'd like ...",
    "en": "Order with I'll have ... or I'd like ..."
   },
   {
    "ko": "정중한 부탁은 Could I have ...?",
    "en": "Polite requests: Could I have ...?"
   },
   {
    "ko": "계산서는 영국에서 bill, 미국에서 check.",
    "en": "The bill is called the check in the US."
   }
  ],
  "examples": [
